/// @namespace eolib
/// Core library for writing Endless Online applications.
///
/// The root namespace holds the error types (eolib::EolibError, eolib::SerializationError and
/// eolib::DeserializationError) and the library version macros in <tt>eolib/version.hpp</tt>. Everything else lives in
/// a nested namespace.

/// @namespace eolib::data
/// Reading and writing EO data.
///
/// eolib::data::EoReader and eolib::data::EoWriter read and write the EO number and string types, and all protocol
/// types are serialized with them. eolib::data::NumberEncoder and eolib::data::StringEncoder expose the underlying
/// encodings, and eolib::data::EoNumericLimits holds the maximum value of each EO number type.

/// @namespace eolib::encrypt
/// Packet encryption and server verification.
///
/// eolib::encrypt::DataEncrypter implements the interleave, flip and swap steps used to encrypt and decrypt packet
/// data, and eolib::encrypt::ServerVerifier hashes the challenge sent by a client during connection initialization.

/// @namespace eolib::packet
/// Packet sequencing.
///
/// eolib::packet::PacketSequencer generates the sequence numbers sent with each client packet. The sequence start
/// types create the initial sequence value from the values sent in the init, account reply and ping packets.

/// @namespace eolib::protocol
/// Types generated from the eo-protocol specification.
///
/// This namespace holds the types shared by the whole protocol, such as eolib::protocol::Coords and
/// eolib::protocol::Direction, and the eolib::protocol::Serializable interface implemented by every generated struct and
/// packet. The nested namespaces follow the layout of the protocol XML files.

/// @namespace eolib::protocol::net
/// Types shared by client and server packets.
///
/// Holds the eolib::protocol::net::Packet interface, the eolib::protocol::net::PacketFamily and
/// eolib::protocol::net::PacketAction enums that identify a packet, and the structs and enums used by both client and
/// server packets.

/// @namespace eolib::protocol::net::client
/// Packets sent by the client, and the structs and enums they use.
///
/// Each packet is named <tt>\<Family\>\<Action\>ClientPacket</tt>. A game server reads them with
/// eolib::protocol::net::client::PacketFactory, which creates the packet for a family and action.

/// @namespace eolib::protocol::net::server
/// Packets sent by the server, and the structs and enums they use.
///
/// Each packet is named <tt>\<Family\>\<Action\>ServerPacket</tt>. A game client reads them with
/// eolib::protocol::net::server::PacketFactory, which creates the packet for a family and action.

/// @namespace eolib::protocol::pub
/// Client pub files: items (eolib::protocol::pub::Eif), NPCs (eolib::protocol::pub::Enf), spells
/// (eolib::protocol::pub::Esf) and classes (eolib::protocol::pub::Ecf), and the records and enums they use.

/// @namespace eolib::protocol::pub::server
/// Server pub files: talk (eolib::protocol::pub::server::TalkFile), shops (eolib::protocol::pub::server::ShopFile),
/// drops (eolib::protocol::pub::server::DropFile), inns (eolib::protocol::pub::server::InnFile) and skill masters
/// (eolib::protocol::pub::server::SkillMasterFile).

/// @namespace eolib::protocol::map
/// Endless Map Files (eolib::protocol::map::Emf), and the structs and enums they use.
